# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Docker build context
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is speed: `target/` and `node_modules/` are
# gigabytes and neither is needed by a Rust build.
#
# The one that matters is that vault shares and .env must never enter a
# build context. Anything in the context can end up in an image layer,
# and image layers get pushed to a registry. A `COPY . .` with a share
# file present publishes key material to GHCR.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Never in an image ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*_shares/
*_share_*.json
share_*.json
*_vault.json
# Password-sealed wallets and the escrow's plaintext signing identity.
nev369_wallet*.json
qlock_attestation.json
keys.json
*.key
*.pem
*.seed
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

# ── Build artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
build/

# ── Not needed by a Rust build ─────────────────────────────────────────
apps/
docs/
monitoring/
nginx/
db/*.md
.github/
*.md
!README.md
deploy.sh
deploy/
Makefile

# ── VCS and tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Local data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
chain.db/
*.sled
data/
pgdata/
tmp/
scratch/
*.log
.DS_Store

.backup-*/
godshield_gateway.json
